# Agentic AI for Financial Requirements Engineering

## Project Goal
An autonomous, collaborative multi-agent AI system to automate requirement gathering, analysis, and SDLC identification specifically for the highly regulated financial sector.

## System Scope
- **Domains:** Digital Banking, Loan Origination, Payment Processing, Fraud Detection, Insurance, Regulatory Reporting, KYC, Financial Analytics.
- **Core Outputs:** SRS, User Stories, Use Cases, Acceptance Criteria, Compliance Mappings, Risk Register, Traceability Matrix, Recommended SDLC Model.

## Multi-Agent Architecture
- **Coordinator Agent:** Workflow control & task assignment.
- **Stakeholder Interaction Agent:** Adaptive interviews & clarification.
- **Requirement Extraction Agent:** Natural language to structured requirements.
- **Clarification Agent:** Ambiguity & gap detection.
- **Classification Agent:** Functional vs Non-Functional (Security, Privacy, etc.).
- **Conflict-Detection Agent:** Contradiction & duplication identification.
- **Compliance Agent:** Mapping to financial regulations & policies.
- **Security & Privacy Agent:** Cybersecurity & privacy requirement identification.
- **Risk-Analysis Agent:** Business & technical risk assessment.
- **SDLC Selection Agent:** Project characteristic analysis & model recommendation.
- **Documentation Agent:** Artifact generation (SRS, Traceability).
- **Validation Agent:** Consistency & evidence verification.
- **Human-Approval Agent:** Routing critical decisions to humans.

## Technical Constraints
- **Groundedness:** Use RAG to prevent hallucinations.
- **Security:** Data masking, RBAC, protection against prompt injection.
- **Traceability:** Every requirement linked to a source stakeholder/document.
- **Human-in-the-loop:** Mandatory for regulatory and high-risk decisions.

